0.2 w 50 738 m 545 738 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 718 Td (1. HISTORICAL EVOLUTION OF ATOMIC STRUCTURE) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 700 Td (Daltons Atomic Theory \(1808\): Matter consists of indivisible atoms.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 685.5 Td (Discovery of Subatomic Particles proved atom is divisible into electrons, protons, and neutrons.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 671.0 Td (Cathode Ray Discharge Tube Experiments \(J.J. Thomson, 1897\): Discovered negatively charged electrons.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 656.5 Td (Charge-to-mass ratio of electron: e/m = 1.758820 x 10^11 C/kg.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 642.0 Td (Millikans Oil Drop Experiment \(1909\): Determined fundamental electronic charge e = -1.6022 x 10^-19 C.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 627.5 Td (Mass of electron: m_e = e / \(e/m\) = 9.1094 x 10^-31 kg.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 605.0 Td (2. ATOMIC MODELS & NUCLEAR DISCOVERY) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 587.0 Td (Thomsons Model of Atom \(Plum Pudding Model\): Uniform sphere of positive charge with electrons embedded.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 572.5 Td (Rutherfords Alpha-Particle Scattering Experiment \(1911\): Gold foil bombarded with fast alpha particles.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 558.0 Td (Key Observation: 99.9% particles passed undeflected; tiny fraction deflected by large angles \(>90 degrees\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 543.5 Td (Conclusion: Atom is mostly empty space; positive charge and mass concentrated in tiny central nucleus.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 529.0 Td (Nuclear radius ~ 10^-15 m compared to atomic radius ~ 10^-10 m.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 514.5 Td (Drawback: Could not explain electronic stability or line spectra of hydrogen.) Tj ET
