0.2 w 50 738 m 545 738 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 718 Td (3. ELECTROMAGNETIC RADIATION & PLANCK S QUANTUM THEORY) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 700 Td (Wave Nature: c = nu x lambda \(c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s in vacuum\). Wave number nu_bar = 1 / lambda.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 685.5 Td (Plancks Quantum Hypothesis \(1900\): Radiant energy emitted or absorbed in discrete packets called quanta.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 671.0 Td (Energy of quantum: E = h x nu = \(h x c\) / lambda, where Planck constant h = 6.626 x 10^-34 J s.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 656.5 Td (Photoelectric Effect \(Hertz, 1887 & Einstein, 1905\): Emission of electrons from metal by light.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 642.0 Td (Kinetic energy of ejected photoelectron: K.E. = h x nu - h x nu_0 = h x nu - W_0 \(Work function\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 619.5 Td (4. BOHR S MODEL FOR HYDROGEN ATOM (1913)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 601.5 Td (Postulate 1: Electrons move in fixed circular orbits called stationary states without radiating energy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 587.0 Td (Postulate 2 \(Quantization of Angular Momentum\): m_e x v x r = n x \(h / 2pi\), where n = 1, 2, 3...) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 572.5 Td (Postulate 3: Energy absorbed or emitted only during orbital transitions: Delta E = E2 - E1 = h x nu.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 558.0 Td (Radius of nth orbit: r_n = \(n^2 x a_0\) / Z, where Bohr radius a_0 = 52.9 pm \(0.529 Angstrom\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 543.5 Td (Energy of nth orbit: E_n = -2.18 x 10^-18 x \(Z^2 / n^2\) J/atom = -13.6 x \(Z^2 / n^2\) eV.) Tj ET
