0.2 w 50 738 m 545 738 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 718 Td (5. HYDROGEN ATOMIC LINE SPECTRA) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 700 Td (Rydberg Formula: nu_bar = 1 / lambda = R_H x Z^2 x [1/\(n1^2\) - 1/\(n2^2\)], R_H = 109,677 cm^-1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 685.5 Td (Lyman Series \(n1 = 1, n2 = 2, 3, 4...\): Ultraviolet \(UV\) region.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 671.0 Td (Balmer Series \(n1 = 2, n2 = 3, 4, 5...\): Visible region of spectrum.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 656.5 Td (Paschen Series \(n1 = 3, n2 = 4, 5...\): Near-Infrared \(IR\) region.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 642.0 Td (Brackett Series \(n1 = 4, n2 = 5, 6...\): Infrared region.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 627.5 Td (Pfund Series \(n1 = 5, n2 = 6, 7...\): Far-Infrared region.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 605.0 Td (6. TOWARDS QUANTUM MECHANICS) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 587.0 Td (Dual Behavior of Matter \(de Broglie, 1924\): lambda = h / p = h / \(m x v\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 572.5 Td (Applicable to microscopic particles \(electrons\) with measurable wave properties.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 558.0 Td (Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle \(1927\): Delta x x Delta p >= h / \(4pi\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 543.5 Td (It is impossible to measure simultaneously both exact position and momentum of a microscopic particle.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 529.0 Td (Significance: Ruled out concept of definitive circular Bohr orbits; established concept of probability.) Tj ET
