BT /F1 16 Tf 50 765 Td (CHAPTER 02: STRUCTURE OF ATOM (PART 4)) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 748 Td (Quantum Numbers, Orbitals & Shapes) Tj ET
0.2 w 50 738 m 545 738 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 718 Td (7. QUANTUM NUMBERS & ORBITAL ADDRESSES) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 700 Td (Principal Quantum Number \(n = 1, 2, 3...\): Determines shell, size, and main orbital energy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 685.5 Td (Azimuthal Quantum Number \(l = 0 to n-1\): Determines subshell and three-dimensional shape.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 671.0 Td (  l = 0 \(s, spherical\); l = 1 \(p, dumbbell\); l = 2 \(d, double dumbbell\); l = 3 \(f, complex\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 656.5 Td (Magnetic Quantum Number \(m_l = -l to +l\): Spatial orientation of orbital. Total orbitals = 2l + 1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 642.0 Td (  s has 1 orbital; p has 3 orbitals \(px, py, pz\); d has 5 orbitals \(dxy, dyz, dzx, dx2-y2, dz2\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 627.5 Td (Spin Quantum Number \(m_s = +1/2 or -1/2\): Spin angular momentum of electron around its own axis.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 605.0 Td (8. NODAL PLANES & PROBABILITY DENSITIES) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 587.0 Td (Radial Nodes = n - l - 1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 572.5 Td (Angular Nodes = l.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 558.0 Td (Total Nodes = \(n - l - 1\) + l = n - 1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 543.5 Td (Example 1: 3p orbital has n=3, l=1 -> Radial nodes = 3-1-1 = 1, Angular nodes = 1, Total = 2.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 529.0 Td (Example 2: 4d orbital has n=4, l=2 -> Radial nodes = 4-2-1 = 1, Angular nodes = 2, Total = 3.) Tj ET
