0.2 w 50 738 m 545 738 l S
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 718 Td (9. RULES FOR FILLING ELECTRONS IN ORBITALS) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 700 Td (Aufbau Principle: Orbitals filled in order of increasing energy: \(n + l\) rule.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 685.5 Td (  Lower \(n + l\) orbital filled first. If \(n + l\) is identical, lower n orbital filled first.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 671.0 Td (  Sequence: 1s < 2s < 2p < 3s < 3p < 4s < 3d < 4p < 5s < 4d < 5p < 6s < 4f < 5d...) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 656.5 Td (Paulis Exclusion Principle: No two electrons in an atom can have the same set of 4 quantum numbers.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 642.0 Td (  Maximum 2 electrons per orbital, and they must have opposite spins \(+1/2 and -1/2\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 627.5 Td (Hunds Rule of Maximum Multiplicity: Pairing in degenerate subshells begins only when each orbital is singly occupied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 613.0 Td (Exceptional Stability: Half-filled \(d5\) and completely-filled \(d10\) subshells have extra symmetry and exchange energy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 598.5 Td (  Chromium \(Z=24\): [Ar] 3d5 4s1 \(not 3d4 4s2\); Copper \(Z=29\): [Ar] 3d10 4s1 \(not 3d9 4s2\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 576.0 Td (10. HIGH-YIELD PRACTICE PROBLEMS & BOARD DERIVATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 558.0 Td (Q1: Calculate wavelength of a photon emitted during transition from n=4 to n=2 in H-atom. \(Ans: 486 nm\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 543.5 Td (Q2: Find the number of radial and angular nodes for 5d orbital. \(Ans: Radial=2, Angular=2\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 529.0 Td (Q3: State why 4s orbital is filled before 3d orbital. Explain using \(n+l\) rule. \(Ans: 4s has n+l=4, 3d has n+l=5\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 514.5 Td (Q4: Calculate de Broglie wavelength of an electron moving with 1% speed of light. \(Ans: 2.42 x 10^-10 m\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 58 500.0 Td (Faculty Mentorship: Senior Chemistry Faculty Dalip Mangotra \(M.Sc Chemistry, B.Ed, CSIR-NET\).) Tj ET
